  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "134",
  "quote": "A landlord is entitled to compensation for the use and occupation of a rental unit by a tenant who does not vacate the rental unit after his or her tenancy is terminated.",
  "reason": "Under sections 86 and 134(3) of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006, a landlord may only collect rent or compensation for the period after a tenancy is terminated if the tenant fails to vacate the unit, and section 134(1) prohibits collecting any unlawful additional charges or penalties. Because this clause requires the tenant to pay for a month after the tenancy has ended and the tenant has vacated, it conflicts with the Act and is void under section 4(1)."
}

